KH2FinalRewrite

The bounded bdscript header/opcode reader in
data/src/bdscript.rs follows OpenKH BdxHeader.cs and
BdxInstructionDescs.cs at commit
7a3b945c538d32c6a285128c98aefba093f52ceb (Apache-2.0), checked against the
selected native interpreter with Ghidra. Bounds and direct control-flow
inspection are owned; this is not an implementation of engine traps,
indirect act callbacks, or installed PC-specific interpreter adjustments.

The package original transform in data/src/original.rs
is adapted from OpenKH EgsEncryption.cs at commit
7a3b945c538d32c6a285128c98aefba093f52ceb under Apache-2.0.
The implementation is modified for bounded byte-wise handling in Rust.
Replacement payload alignment follows EgsHdAsset.cs at the same pin;
complete explicit selection adds count and cumulative allocation bounds.
HD image decoding uses image 0.25.10/png 0.18.1 and crc32fast 1.5.2
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), with owned range/profile checks. The codec feature graph
uses zlib-rs 0.6.8 (Zlib); its unchanged notice is retained in
docs/release/zlib-rs-LICENSE.txt. Full dependency attribution remains a release
qualification requirement.
The bounded legacy DDS BGRA8 route preserves byte channels using the standard
32-bit A8R8G8B8 masks. Its explicit straight-RGBA profile is checked against
unchanged private DirectXTex LoadScanline BGRA/StoreScanline RGBA case statements
at 1acf4ebe6330e06b7eb52e8db63d4f824ad77427 (Microsoft, MIT). Public source and
compiled research adapters remain outside Git/distribution; row/pitch/surface
exclusions are owned inspection bounds, not a complete DDS format claim.
The explicit legacy BC3 mip-chain inspection profile follows the standard DDS
surface layout, checked against unchanged DirectXTex ComputePitch BC3 normal
branch and MulOverflow at the same Microsoft pin. Pixel arithmetic retains the
explicit normalized CPU profile checked against unchanged DecodeBC1/D3DXDecodeBC3
and DirectXMath UNORM8 storage. Private public extracts/binaries remain external;
complete-chain bounds and output envelopes are owned. This does not qualify
installed filtering, material routing, hardware rounding or runtime behavior.
The room COCT v1 raw-record reader adapts Coct.cs at the OpenKH pin above,
preserving float bits, flags and table/graph indices with added bounds checks.
Its explicit polygon display topology follows MapStudio CollisionModel.cs;
it does not define installed movement or collision response rules.
Room visual geometry follows Model.cs, ModelBackground.cs and MdlxParser.cs
at the same OpenKH pin. Stateful VIF upload observation preserves memory/mask
between microprogram stops; it does not execute VU code. Map packet views
follow VpuPacket.cs. Added limits/rejection paths and Bevy scene code are owned.
Candidate name generation in tools/Compare-CandidateNames.ps1 follows
the KH2-only EgsTools rules at the same pin; upstream catalogs are
referenced privately and are not included in this repository.
The bounded interpolated-motion reader adapts Motion.cs at the same OpenKH pin.
Complete keys and alignment tails remain separate; constraint/helper/root and
expression structures are retained without claiming installed evaluation.
Explicit basic FK sampling follows legacy Motion.Read, Kh2MotionEngine.cs and
MathEx.cs, with added bounds and rejection of undefined zero-duration results.
It ignores scale, inverse curves, IK, constraints, expressions, root motion and
triggers just as the selected basic consumer does; no installed clock is chosen.
Retained skin bindings reuse the explicit public pose arithmetic above. Native
preview frame stepping, mesh updates and finite capture tours are owned code.
The explicit sequential trigger-record profile additionally follows the
MotionTrigger.cs constructor at the same pin. Declared offsets, signed frames,
unknown IDs and trailing bytes are retained; widths beyond four parameters
reject rather than truncating. No installed event behavior is inferred.
The bounded message-record reader follows Msg.Read/GetMsgData at the
same OpenKH pin, retaining encoded spans without a glyph dictionary.
System-message token boundaries additionally follow the pinned system decoder
length table. The differing command 0x17 length is retained as an explicit
research conflict; installed runtime semantics and Unicode are not asserted.
The optional explicit International-system text profile follows the public
InternationalSystemDecode table and BaseMessageDecoder text grouping at that
same pin. Complex symbols and original encoded spans remain distinct;
unsupported slots and unmapped tables are preserved without fabricated text.
Optional public-profile re-encoding follows InternationalSystemEncode at the
same pin, paired with original borrowed spans and explicit unmapped exclusions.
Public unsupported-value aliases are observations, never source replacements.
The localized font plane/palette decoder follows RawBitmap.cs,
Contextes/FontContext.cs and Ps2.Utility.cs/Ps2.Repl.cs at that pin.
The Rust decoder adds strict plane/palette length checks and private previews.
Explicit font-cell candidate coordinates follow Constants.cs and the
Kh2MessageRenderer DrawChar methods at the same pin, with added bounds and
non-aliased bank checks. Original spacing bytes remain uninterpreted;
public profile coordinates do not assert installed runtime glyph behavior.
Bounded model structure and DMA selection follow Mdlx.Model.cs at that pin.
The explicit CPU VIF profile in vif.rs adapts VifUnpacker.cs for bounded Rust
first-run, zero-TOPS execution while retaining the public reader's behavior.
Raw type-1 VU data ranges follow VpuPacket.cs; bounds, integer bit preservation
and format exclusions are added. The explicit type-1 topology profile follows
VpuPacketExtensions.cs and
Kkdf2MdlxParser.cs at that pin, adding association/index/ring/allocation checks.
Topology retains the public integer UV truncation and first-submodel scope;
Installed bind matrices, skinning, materials and rendering stay open.
Explicit inspection bind routes in model_pose.rs follow the public
BuildTPoseMatrices/GetBoneMatrices and Kkdf2 single/multi expressions.
Numerical FMA ordering and quaternion/matrix formulas adapt .NET runtime
60629d14374c56f1cb51819049ad1fa529307f8d under MIT; its notice is retained in
docs/release/dotnet-runtime-LICENSE.txt. Rust sin/cos and finite comparisons
do not select installed rendering, authoritative simulation or a tolerance.
Neither CPU profile nor model observations
assert PS2 hardware, installed transforms, shadow geometry or gameplay fidelity.
The explicit bounded model-texture layout/CLUT profile follows ModelTexture.cs,
Tm2.cs and Ps2.Utility.cs at the same OpenKH pin. Raw transfer/environment words,
indexed image spans, palette addressing and alpha conversion remain separate
from pixel swizzle, HD replacement routing, footer animation and installed GS
behavior. Footer spans follow TextureFooterData.cs/UvScroll.cs without decoding
animation or assigning unknown payload meaning.
The explicit indexed model-texture pixel profile additionally adapts
Texture.GetData and Ps2.Reform32.cs/Ps2.Reform8.cs/Ps2.Reform4.cs at that pin.
Encode32 is a pure memory byte rearrangement in this route. Complete page,
dimension, length and allocation bounds are added; indexed4 output preserves
the public high-nibble-first packing. CPU equality does not qualify installed
GS sampling, HD material routing, texture animation or shader behavior.
The explicit model texture-link inspection profile adapts EgsTools.RAW offset
formulas and TextureAnimation header/stride at the same OpenKH pin. It reads
only bounded recognized footer chunks instead of the public whole-payload
signature scan. Exact replacement offsets remain raw; unmatched or ambiguous
links are retained. Geometry associations retain Kkdf2 global UV references
and the GraphicsDeviceExtensions 16-bit texture-index mask. This does not
select the installed UV route or interpret high replacement-offset flags.
Textured model inspection adapts both pinned public UV expressions while
retaining Kkdf2 topology. The signed16 expression does not incorporate the
whole legacy parser. Original/exact HD bindings and diagnostic presentation
choices remain explicit; source mip levels and TEXA metadata are retained
without inferred sampling, material or animation behavior.
The explicit bounded TEXA record profile additionally adapts the read-only
TextureFooterData constructor, TextureFrame getters and BitsUtil.SignExtend
at the same OpenKH pin. Fixed-size frame graphs and signed slots remain
observations; body/allocation/visit bounds are added. Unknown controls and raw
duration/sprite/header values remain retained. No playback, timer, slot or
installed animation behavior is inferred.

The bounded PRTY inspection reader additionally follows PrtyFile.Read at the
same pin, retaining distinct raw offset records after the first table slot.
Header-overlapping records are exposed explicitly. Character mappings, units
and runtime movement rules are not inferred from these records.

