The PTYA attack-set and 00objentry readers follow the public layouts in
OpenKH docs/kh2/file/type/00battle.md and Objentry.cs at the pin above; the
motion slot chooser follows MotionSet.GetMotionSetIndex. Range-trigger IDs
honoured by the test room follow docs/kh2/file/anb/anb.md and COCT surface
flag bits follow docs/kh2/file/type/coct.md. These are public labels; the
test-room controller does not claim installed movement or combat rules.
The motion evaluator in data/src/motion_eval.rs reads the IK
helper, joint order, constraint, limiter, expression and root-position tables
using the layouts in OpenKH docs/kh2/file/anb/motion.md (pin above) and
kenjiuno's msetDoc README (gitlab.com/kenjiuno/msetDoc). No code was copied;
the solver rules are this project's own and are recorded as inferences in T057.

The combat rules in the player controller were checked against the KH2 Combat
Kit by steferro78 (https://github.com/steferro78-HIV/kh2-combat-kit, MIT).
No code or data from that project is copied. It was reviewed and used only as a
cross-check for the variable-height jump and the Square-button moves (T105).
The ported behaviour follows the decompiled exe routines cited in the code.

The LAN duel's KH3 ruleset (player::kh3, T279) follows the behaviour described
by kingdom-hearts-x-elden-ring by StrawHatPro
(https://github.com/StrawHatPro/kingdom-hearts-x-elden-ring, MIT, Copyright (c)
2026 StrawHatPro; the licence text is in CREDITS.md). Its movement, flowmotion,
combo homing, focus and shotlock behaviour and tuning numbers were reimplemented
in this project's code. For the KH3 mode (T282): its readers' formats were
reimplemented in source/data/src/kh3 (pak, package, tagged properties, skeletal and
static meshes, animations, textures, SEAD, HCA), its attack and magic states in
source/game/player/src/kh3, and its crates/kh-vfx was ported, with its notice kept,
as source/visual/effect/src/cascade. For the KH3 ruleset's 1:1 pass (T300): its crates/kh-core
was ported as source/game/kh3_sora, the KineDriver and Bonamik solvers of its crates/kh-anim as
source/game/kh3_rig, and the auto SE detector of its crates/kh-audio as
source/main/src/test_room/kh3_autose.rs. Its generated tables and anything embedding
KH3 data were not copied, and no KH3 data is in this repository: the KH3 mode
reads the player's own install at run time.
